;;=============================================================================
;; SpiceColourTest.tdl  —  TEMPORARY PROBE.  Load, print, unload.
;;=============================================================================
;; ONE QUESTION: does `Print BG` put colour on paper on THIS machine at all?
;;
;; In SpiceLetterheadInvoice.tdl the green bands never appear. Two very
;; different reasons are still possible and they need opposite fixes:
;;
;;   a) `Print BG` works here, but not inside a from-scratch [Report:] —
;;      in which case the letterhead has to be rebuilt on Tally's own invoice
;;      format to get colour (and probably the QR with it)
;;
;;   b) `Print BG` produces nothing on this machine regardless — a printer,
;;      driver or print-mode limitation — in which case NO amount of TDL will
;;      ever make those bands green, and we stop trying
;;
;; This file tints ONE band on Tally's BUILT-IN invoice. That is exactly the
;; construct the site's own Customized Invoice.txt uses in production:
;;
;;     [#Part: EXPINV Column]
;;         Print BG:Black
;;
;; so if colour can print here, it will print here.
;;
;;-----------------------------------------------------------------------------
;; HOW TO USE
;;   1. F1 > TDL & Add-on > F4 (Manage Local TDLs) — ADD this file.
;;      Leave SpiceLetterheadInvoice.tdl loaded; they touch different things.
;;   2. Restart Tally.
;;   3. Open ANY sales invoice and print it with Tally's OWN format —
;;      Ctrl+P, the normal print. NOT Alt+L, which is the letterhead layout.
;;   4. Look at the column-header row (Description / Quantity / Rate / Amount).
;;
;;        GREEN band   -> answer (a): colour works, the custom report is the
;;                        blocker, and the rebuild is worth doing
;;        still white  -> answer (b): colour cannot print here at all, and the
;;                        green requirement has to be dropped or the printer
;;                        changed
;;
;;   5. REMOVE this file from Manage Local TDLs afterwards — it recolours the
;;      standard invoice, which you do not want left on.
;;-----------------------------------------------------------------------------

[#Part: EXPINV Column]

    Print BG : Light Green
